From 3fc650b6426c3c26c3775a37c2c8b93ef84a97ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:12:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 52/57] hw/sensor: BME280 humidity, pressure and temperature,
 the Weather Click

bme280 on I2C at 0x76: the register map with a typical calibration
image, sleep, forced and normal modes with the typical measurement times
and the standby times, oversampling resolution, the IIR filter, skipped
readings, results held back during a burst read, the 0xB6 reset. The raw
readings come from bisection over the data sheet's integer compensation,
so firmware compensating them reads "temperature", "pressure" and
"humidity" back. SPI is not modelled. qtest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
